{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBfyp7deNhyG7iMTGtYDNq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Ralph Fix Plan\n     2→\n     3→## High Priority\n     4→- [ ] **Middleware** (`src/middleware.ts`) — redirects unauthenticated requests to `/login` at the edge. This protects all `(dashboard)` routes without any per-page code.\n     5→- [ ] **Dashboard layout** (`src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`) — calls `auth()` once, fetches the session, and makes user info available to all child pages (via props or a context provider). Individual pages do **not** call `requireAuth()`.\n     6→- [ ] **Server actions** (`src/lib/actions/*.ts`) — each action still calls `requireAuth()` at the top. Mutations must always re-verify auth independently of the UI.\n     7→- [ ] **API routes** (`src/app/api/v1/...`) — use API key auth (see Phase 1.5), not session auth.\n     8→- [ ] Start Postgres: `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d`\n     9→- [ ] Run migration: `npx prisma migrate dev --name init`\n    10→- [ ] Seed database: `npx prisma db seed`\n    11→- [ ] Start dev server: `npm run dev`\n    12→- [ ] Test auth: login with admin@example.com / admin123, verify redirect to dashboard\n    13→- [ ] Test session revocation: logout, verify session is deleted from DB, verify protected pages redirect\n    14→- [ ] Test properties: create property, add units, edit, delete\n    15→- [ ] Test tenants: create tenant, verify list\n    16→- [ ] Test leases: create lease linking tenant to unit, verify unit status changes to OCCUPIED\n    17→- [ ] Test billing: generate rent charges for current month, verify charges appear\n    18→- [ ] Test payments: record payment, verify it allocates to oldest charge, verify charge status updates\n    19→- [ ] Test REST API: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/properties` — verify JSON response\n    20→- [ ] Test API create: POST to `/api/v1/tenants` with valid payload, verify 201 response\n    21→- [ ] Test API auth: request without API key returns 401\n    22→\n    23→\n    24→## Medium Priority\n    25→\n    26→\n    27→## Low Priority\n    28→\n    29→\n    30→## Completed\n    31→- [x] Project enabled for Ralph\n    32→\n    33→## Notes\n    34→- Focus on MVP functionality first\n    35→- Ensure each feature is properly tested\n    36→- Update this file after each major milestone\n    37→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cda4584-66ff-4fc5-abc8-e5e58a360333","uuid":"0b50ec7b-61b9-4a47-aaad-ee32c70c3a4c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Volumes/Secondary/workspace/tenant-portal/.ralph/fix_plan.md","content":"# Ralph Fix Plan\n\n## High Priority\n- [ ] **Middleware** (`src/middleware.ts`) — redirects unauthenticated requests to `/login` at the edge. This protects all `(dashboard)` routes without any per-page code.\n- [ ] **Dashboard layout** (`src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`) — calls `auth()` once, fetches the session, and makes user info available to all child pages (via props or a context provider). Individual pages do **not** call `requireAuth()`.\n- [ ] **Server actions** (`src/lib/actions/*.ts`) — each action still calls `requireAuth()` at the top. Mutations must always re-verify auth independently of the UI.\n- [ ] **API routes** (`src/app/api/v1/...`) — use API key auth (see Phase 1.5), not session auth.\n- [ ] Start Postgres: `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d`\n- [ ] Run migration: `npx prisma migrate dev --name init`\n- [ ] Seed database: `npx prisma db seed`\n- [ ] Start dev server: `npm run dev`\n- [ ] Test auth: login with admin@example.com / admin123, verify redirect to dashboard\n- [ ] Test session revocation: logout, verify session is deleted from DB, verify protected pages redirect\n- [ ] Test properties: create property, add units, edit, delete\n- [ ] Test tenants: create tenant, verify list\n- [ ] Test leases: create lease linking tenant to unit, verify unit status changes to OCCUPIED\n- [ ] Test billing: generate rent charges for current month, verify charges appear\n- [ ] Test payments: record payment, verify it allocates to oldest charge, verify charge status updates\n- [ ] Test REST API: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/properties` — verify JSON response\n- [ ] Test API create: POST to `/api/v1/tenants` with valid payload, verify 201 response\n- [ ] Test API auth: request without API key returns 401\n\n\n## Medium Priority\n\n\n## Low Priority\n\n\n## Completed\n- [x] Project enabled for Ralph\n\n## Notes\n- Focus on MVP functionality first\n- Ensure each feature is properly tested\n- Update this file after each major milestone\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
